What is Pseudocode + Example
Pseudocode is a plain-language description of an algorithm. It’s not real code, so you don’t worry about syntax. It helps you plan logic before writing in Python, Java, etc.
Simple example: Check if a number is even
BEGIN
    INPUT number
    IF number MOD 2 = 0 THEN
        PRINT “Even”
    ELSE
        PRINT “Odd”
    END IF
END
`MOD` means remainder after division. If remainder is 0, the number is even.

